      ],
      "acceptable_supporting": []
    },
    "description": "The Checkout service calls the external inventory system for each order line. CheckoutService depends on an ordinary StockLookup interface whose checkStock(sku) method returns a typed StockResult. The current integration uses a request-reply broker topic: each request must identify its destination, carry a correlation identifier and reply address, wait up to 800 ms, parse the response, and translate connection failures into an unavailable-stock result. An InventoryGateway implementation owns those details and invokes InventoryService for incoming replies. CheckoutService must not construct broker envelopes, select queues, inspect acknowledgements, or understand correlation metadata. A timeout must produce a deterministic local result, a retry must reuse the same correlation identifier, and malformed replies must be logged as integration errors without reaching the checkout business rules. The inventory system remains independently deployable and exposes no shared in-process interface.",
    "decision_statement": "Should inventory access be represented as a typed domain method behind a component that owns request construction, correlation, timeout handling, and response translation?",
    "notes": "messaging-gateway fits the typed StockLookup method hiding request-reply correlation and timeouts; service-activator covers the reply-invocation angle and message-endpoint the generic seam."
  },
